Subject: main: the default temporary directory is /sys$scratch on OpenVMS

With TMPDIR unset, sys_get_temp_dir() falls back to P_tmpdir, which the
OpenVMS C RTL defines as "SYS$SCRATCH:", a VMS device specification.
PHP joins it to file names with '/', so session files became
"SYS$SCRATCH:/sess_..." and open() failed with ENOENT: 159 session tests
and the file tests that use tempnam() (vms-php PORTING_LOG #25).  On VMS
default to "/sys$scratch", the same directory in UNIX syntax (as patch
0005 does for opcache's lock file).  TMPDIR and sys_temp_dir still take
precedence.
---
--- a/main/php_open_temporary_file.c
+++ b/main/php_open_temporary_file.c
@@ -295,6 +295,12 @@
 			return PG(php_sys_temp_dir);
 		}
 	}
+#ifdef __VMS
+	/* The C RTL's P_tmpdir is "SYS$SCRATCH:", a VMS device spec that PHP
+	 * would join to names with '/': use its UNIX form. */
+	PG(php_sys_temp_dir) = estrdup("/sys$scratch");
+	return PG(php_sys_temp_dir);
+#endif
 #ifdef P_tmpdir
 	/* Use the standard default temporary directory. */
 	if (P_tmpdir) {
